The free-algebra concern is real: choosing the defining polynomial gives arbitrary \(N\) a small-degree compression, and its norms need not have \(N\)-sized lifts. In the examples I’ve checked, however, the relation already holds over \(\mathbf Z\), so taking norms gives an exact integer equality. That is a narrower obstruction than §§5.5–5.6 claim.
